Select a resolution the sink will actually render.

Upstream #if 0'd this whole block, so every session ran at a hardcoded
1920x1080@30. Its comment condemns only codec->native ("the native resolution
reported by some devices is just useless"), but the bitmask-decoded list went
with it.

Trust codec->native first. Ranking the advertised list by pixel count is wrong
for an LG webOS panel, which declares native 1920x1080@60 yet omits that mode
from the selected codec's own 37-entry list, leaving 1920x1200@30 on top -- a
16:10 30Hz mode it accepts during negotiation and then never renders, showing a
loading screen for the whole session. Both sinks tested report a native that is
correct; ranking only wins when there is no native to trust.

GND_FORCE_RESOLUTION=WIDTHxHEIGHT@RATE overrides the choice, and
GND_FALLBACK_RESOLUTION still covers sinks that advertise empty CEA/VESA/HH
masks and no native.

Not upstreamed.

